<title>AUSTRIA: No need for early OPEC talks on Iraq - Rakad.</title>
<headline>No need for early OPEC talks on Iraq - Rakad.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Acting UAE oil minister Rakad bin Salem bin Rakad said on Tuesday that he saw no reason to have an early OPEC meeting to discuss renewed Iraqi exports ahead of the group's scheduled meeting in June next year.</p>
<p>Asked if OPEC would meet earlier than June on the issue, Rakad, also OPEC President, said &quot;no, I believe it (the group's schedule) will remain normal.&quot;</p>
<p>Asked whether the market could absorb OPEC's current output and the possible return of Iraqi oil early next year, he said &quot;yes, definitely i believe it (the market) will remain as it is.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
</text>
